"use strict";(self.webpackChunkimport_ean_upc_barcodes_doc=self.webpackChunkimport_ean_upc_barcodes_doc||[]).push([[128],{930(e,o,a){a.r(o),a.d(o,{comp:()=>l,data:()=>s});var t=a(641);const n=[(0,t.Fv)('<h1 id="managing-the-barcode-pool" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#managing-the-barcode-pool"><span>Managing the Barcode Pool</span></a></h1><p>When you upload sequential files, the barcodes are stored in a centralized pool table within the WordPress database. You can manage this pool directly from the <strong>Import Codes</strong> tab.</p><h2 id="batch-tracking" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#batch-tracking"><span>Batch Tracking</span></a></h2><p>The plugin organizes your imported pool into distinct batches based on your file uploads. On the Import Codes tab, you will see a table displaying:</p><ul><li><strong>Batch Date/Time:</strong> When the file was uploaded.</li><li><strong>Filename:</strong> The name of the original uploaded file.</li><li><strong>Total Codes:</strong> The total number of valid codes extracted from the file.</li><li><strong>Used Codes:</strong> How many codes from this specific batch have been assigned to products.</li><li><strong>Available Codes:</strong> How many codes are left to be assigned.</li></ul><h2 id="multi-file-continuation" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#multi-file-continuation"><span>Multi-File Continuation</span></a></h2><p>One of the most important features of the pool system is <strong>Multi-file continuation</strong>.</p><p>You do not need to manually track which barcode you used last. When one uploaded file runs out of available codes during a bulk assignment or over time as new products are created, you simply upload the next file.</p><p>The assignment process will continue seamlessly from the new batch without any conflicts, ensuring a continuous supply of barcodes for your store.</p><h2 id="pool-cleanup" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#pool-cleanup"><span>Pool Cleanup</span></a></h2><p>If you ever upload an incorrect file or decide to change your barcode provider, you can clean up the unused codes.</p><ul><li><strong>Delete Unused Codes:</strong> Each batch row in the table includes a &quot;Delete&quot; action. Clicking this will remove all <em>unassigned</em> codes belonging to that specific batch from the pool.</li><li><strong>Safe Deletion:</strong> The plugin will never delete a code that has already been assigned to a product. Deleting a batch only removes the remaining available stock from the pool.</li></ul>',12)],i={},l=(0,a(6262).A)(i,[["render",function(e,o){return(0,t.uX)(),(0,t.CE)("div",null,n)}]]),s=JSON.parse('{"path":"/guide/managing-pool.html","title":"Managing the Pool","lang":"en-US","frontmatter":{"title":"Managing the Pool"},"headers":[{"level":2,"title":"Batch Tracking","slug":"batch-tracking","link":"#batch-tracking","children":[]},{"level":2,"title":"Multi-File Continuation","slug":"multi-file-continuation","link":"#multi-file-continuation","children":[]},{"level":2,"title":"Pool Cleanup","slug":"pool-cleanup","link":"#pool-cleanup","children":[]}],"git":{},"filePathRelative":"guide/managing-pool.md"}')}}]);